      "input_bytes": 1590,
      "input_storage": "inline",
      "text": "All five steps completed in order.\n\n## Command stdout\n\n1. `echo \"subagent-marker-one\"` → `subagent-marker-one`\n2. `node /home/USER/Desktop/agent-lens/experiments/tracer-bullet/emit.mjs 1KB` → a synthetic filler stream: `<<@000000000>>` followed by dots, then `<<@000000512>>` followed by dots. The file existed at the expected path — no discrepancy.\n3. `echo \"subagent-marker-three\"` → `subagent-marker-three`\n\n## emit.mjs byte count\n\n**1024 bytes (1 KB).** The script embeds zero-padded byte-offset markers (`<<@NNNNNNNNN>>`, 14 bytes each) every 512 bytes and pads the remainder with `.`. Two markers appeared, at offsets `000000000` and `000000512`, each followed by 498 dots — 512 + 512 = 1024 bytes, matching the requested `1KB` argument exactly. Nothing was truncated in what I observed.\n\n## Nested sub-agent report (verbatim)\n\n```\nRan the single command as instructed.\n\nstdout was exactly:\n\n```\nnested-marker\n```\n```\n\nThe nested agent (id `abf92dc8635043dac`) used 1 tool call, 20,800 subagent tokens, 4,248 ms.\nagentId: a08c8cbbc57139aa2 (use SendMessage with to: 'a08c8cbbc57139aa2', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 22770\ntool_uses: 4\nduration_ms: 27138</usage>",
